{"seq":16,"slug":"game-theory","title":"博弈论","stage":"DONE","category":"mathematics-statistics","chapterCount":5,"docCount":16,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory","rating":{"composite":3.97,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4.4,"coverage":3.25,"positioning":5,"strategic":3.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"博弈论\">博弈论</h1><p>博弈论研究理性决策者之间的策略互动：当多个参与者的选择彼此影响、每个人的最优决策又取决于他人的决策时，单人最优化方法便失效——博弈论正是为分析这类「互动决策」而生。本 hub 把博弈论当作一门<strong>数学理论</strong>来讲：从博弈的精确定义出发，建立纳什均衡这一核心解概念，再扩展到动态、重复、混合策略与不完全信息，最后纵览其跨学科应用与局限。重点是讲清「概念为什么这样定义、解概念为什么这样构造」，而非堆砌某一行业的案例。</p>\n<h2 id=\"本-hub-的定位-和它的-兄弟-们如何分工\">本 hub 的定位：和它的「兄弟」们如何分工</h2><p>博弈论是天然的跨学科主题，本仓库里有多个 hub 从不同角度触及它。读之前先认清边界，避免走错门：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Hub</th>\n<th>侧重</th>\n<th>什么时候读它</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>本 hub（数学·博弈论）</strong></td>\n<td>概念的<strong>数学结构与解概念</strong>：均衡为何存在、如何求解、不同精炼之间的逻辑</td>\n<td>想从第一性原理理解博弈论本身，打通用基础</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../../economics-finance/game-theory/\">经济学·博弈论</a></td>\n<td>同一套概念的<strong>经济学应用</strong>：寡头、拍卖、议价、商业策略，案例密集</td>\n<td>已懂基本概念，想看它在市场与企业中怎么用</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../../economics-finance/information-economics/\">信息经济学</a></td>\n<td><strong>信息不对称</strong>的专门理论：逆向选择、道德风险、信号与甄别</td>\n<td>想深挖「不完全信息」这一支，超出本 hub 第五章的广度</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../../economics-finance/market-design-mechanism-design/\">市场设计与机制设计</a></td>\n<td><strong>反向工程</strong>：设计规则让自利行为导向目标，拍卖、匹配市场</td>\n<td>想从「分析博弈」走向「设计博弈」</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../../ai-llm/reinforcement-learning/multi-agent-rl/marl-foundations\">强化学习·多智能体</a></td>\n<td>博弈均衡作为<strong>多智能体学习</strong>的目标与动力学</td>\n<td>关心博弈论在 AI / 自我博弈中的现代落地</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../../biology-life-science/evolutionary-biology/\">进化生物学</a></td>\n<td>博弈逻辑支配<strong>无意识的生物演化</strong>：进化稳定策略</td>\n<td>关心鹰鸽博弈、ESS 等生物学应用</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>一句话：<strong>本 hub 教你「博弈论是什么、为什么」，兄弟 hub 教你「在某个领域怎么用」。</strong> 应用类 hub 与本 hub 在基本概念上有意重叠，但本 hub 给的是统一、严格的母本。</p>\n<h2 id=\"章节结构\">章节结构</h2><ul>\n<li><strong>第一章 基础与基本要素</strong>：博弈的定义、参与者—策略—收益三要素、理性与共同知识假设、博弈的分类与两种表示形式（标准式 / 扩展式）。</li>\n<li><strong>第二章 标准式博弈与纳什均衡</strong>：收益矩阵、占优策略、最优反应，并深入剖析整个理论的基石——纳什均衡（稳定性、存在性、多重性）。</li>\n<li><strong>第三章 经典博弈模型</strong>：囚徒困境、协调博弈、鹰鸽博弈与公地悲剧，揭示个体理性与集体福利的张力。</li>\n<li><strong>第四章 动态博弈与重复博弈</strong>：博弈树、逆向归纳、子博弈完美均衡、可信威胁与承诺，以及合作如何在「未来的影子」下涌现。</li>\n<li><strong>第五章 进阶与应用</strong>：混合策略、不完全信息（贝叶斯博弈），并纵览经济、生物、政治、AI 中的应用及理论的意义与局限。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"推荐学习路径-分人群\">推荐学习路径（分人群）</h2><ul>\n<li><strong>数学 / 理论方向（系统打基础）</strong>：严格按章节顺序 1→2→3→4→5。第二章的纳什均衡是枢纽，务必吃透「互为最优反应」与存在性定理；之后第四、五章都建立在它之上。</li>\n<li><strong>经济 / 管理方向（重应用）</strong>：先读第一、二、三章建立直觉（尤其囚徒困境、协调、公地悲剧），第四章重点看「可信承诺」，第五章看不完全信息与应用一节，然后切到 <a href=\"../../economics-finance/game-theory/\">经济学·博弈论</a> 与 <a href=\"../../economics-finance/market-design-mechanism-design/\">市场设计</a> 深耕案例。</li>\n<li><strong>AI / 算法方向</strong>：通读第一、二章建立解概念，重点读第四章（动态/重复博弈对应序贯决策）与第五章混合策略，然后转 <a href=\"../../ai-llm/reinforcement-learning/multi-agent-rl/marl-foundations\">强化学习·多智能体</a>。</li>\n<li><strong>只想要直觉（通识阅读）</strong>：读第一章 1.1、第二章纳什均衡、第三章全部、第五章意义与局限——四篇即可建立对「策略互动」的核心认识。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"前置知识\">前置知识</h2><ul>\n<li><strong>必需</strong>：会读简单的表格与不等式；理解「函数把输入映射到输出」。本 hub 的标准式博弈、占优分析、纯策略纳什均衡几乎不需要更多。</li>\n<li><strong>第五章混合策略 / 不完全信息</strong>：需要<a href=\"../probability-statistics/\">概率与期望</a>的基础——概率分布、期望值、<a href=\"../probability-statistics/probability-foundations/bayes-theorem\">贝叶斯定理</a>（用于信念更新）。</li>\n<li><strong>进阶理解（可选）</strong>：纳什均衡的存在性证明用到不动点定理，零和博弈的极小极大与<a href=\"../optimization-theory/convex-optimization/duality-theory\">凸优化的对偶/鞍点</a>同源——想深究均衡为何「一定存在」时再补。</li>\n<li><strong>关于「理性」</strong>：本 hub 默认参与者完全理性且这是共同知识。这是理想化前提；想了解真实决策如何偏离，可参考<a href=\"../../economics-finance/behavioral-economics/\">行为经济学</a>。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>始终把握一条主线：<strong>博弈论研究的是「我的最优选择取决于你的选择，而你的选择又取决于我的」这种相互依存的策略情境</strong>——理解这种互动的逻辑，是认识竞争与合作、个体与集体之深刻关系的钥匙。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础与基本要素","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"what-is-a-game","title":"什么是博弈","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/foundations/what-is-a-game"},{"seq":2,"slug":"basic-elements","title":"博弈的基本要素","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/foundations/basic-elements"},{"seq":3,"slug":"rationality-and-representations","title":"理性假设、分类与表示","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/foundations/rationality-and-representations"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"normal-form-and-nash","title":"标准式博弈与纳什均衡","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/normal-form-and-nash","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"payoff-matrix-and-dominance","title":"收益矩阵与占优策略","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/normal-form-and-nash/payoff-matrix-and-dominance"},{"seq":2,"slug":"best-response","title":"最优反应","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/normal-form-and-nash/best-response"},{"seq":3,"slug":"nash-equilibrium","title":"纳什均衡","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/normal-form-and-nash/nash-equilibrium"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"classic-games","title":"经典博弈模型","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/classic-games","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"prisoners-dilemma","title":"囚徒困境","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/classic-games/prisoners-dilemma"},{"seq":2,"slug":"coordination-games","title":"协调博弈","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/classic-games/coordination-games"},{"seq":3,"slug":"hawk-dove-and-commons","title":"鹰鸽博弈与公地悲剧","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/classic-games/hawk-dove-and-commons"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"dynamic-and-repeated","title":"动态博弈与重复博弈","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/dynamic-and-repeated","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"game-trees-backward-induction","title":"博弈树与逆向归纳","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/dynamic-and-repeated/game-trees-backward-induction"},{"seq":2,"slug":"subgame-perfect-credible-threats","title":"子博弈完美与可信威胁","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/dynamic-and-repeated/subgame-perfect-credible-threats"},{"seq":3,"slug":"repeated-games-cooperation","title":"重复博弈与合作","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/dynamic-and-repeated/repeated-games-cooperation"}]},{"seq":5,"slug":"advanced-and-applications","title":"进阶与应用","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/advanced-and-applications","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"mixed-strategy","title":"混合策略","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/advanced-and-applications/mixed-strategy"},{"seq":2,"slug":"incomplete-information","title":"不完全信息博弈","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/advanced-and-applications/incomplete-information"},{"seq":3,"slug":"applications","title":"博弈论的应用","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/advanced-and-applications/applications"},{"seq":4,"slug":"significance-and-limits","title":"博弈论的意义与局限","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/game-theory/advanced-and-applications/significance-and-limits"}]}]}